From: Apollo port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5k3t2, s5k5e9: cap analogue gain at the OEM 16x limit

Both original Apollo sensor libraries clamp analogue gain to 16x before
encoding it in unsigned Q5. The wide S5KHMX instead allows 32x. Keep that
difference in the V4L2 controls rather than sending an unsupported 32x value
to the front and macro sensors.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3t2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k3t2.c
@@ -48,5 +48,5 @@
 #define S5K3T2_REG_AGAIN		CCI_REG16(0x0204)
 #define S5K3T2_AGAIN_MIN		32
-#define S5K3T2_AGAIN_MAX		1024
+#define S5K3T2_AGAIN_MAX		512
 #define S5K3T2_AGAIN_STEP		1
 #define S5K3T2_AGAIN_DEFAULT		32
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/s5k5e9.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/s5k5e9.c
@@ -48,5 +48,5 @@
 #define S5K5E9_REG_AGAIN		CCI_REG16(0x0204)
 #define S5K5E9_AGAIN_MIN		32
-#define S5K5E9_AGAIN_MAX		1024
+#define S5K5E9_AGAIN_MAX		512
 #define S5K5E9_AGAIN_STEP		1
 #define S5K5E9_AGAIN_DEFAULT		32
